d bet by 1000.\n* On Round 2, your opponent performed action: 0.\n* On Round 3, your opponent performed action: 0.\nYour valid actions are: [-2 (All-in), -1 (Fold), 0 (Check), 100 (raise the bet), or any value above 100 but lower than your current chips.].\n', 'reasoning': '', 'output': "Evaluation: I have a strong two-pair hand: Aces and Tens with a Queen kicker. The board shows Ace of Clubs, 10 of Clubs, 10 of Spades, 3 of Diamonds, Queen of Clubs. My hole cards are Ace of Hearts and 3 of Spades, giving me two pair (Aces and Tens) plus a lower pair of 3s, but the best five-card hand is A-A-10-10-Q. There's a flush draw on the board (three clubs), but I don't have a club. My opponent has checked on every round so far, indicating weakness or a slow-play. Since it's the river and all cards are out, I can value bet to extract chips. Going all-in might be excessive and could scare off a weaker hand. A moderate raise seems best.\n\nReason: My hand is very strong—two pair with top pair and top kicker. The opponent's consistent checking suggests they likely have a weaker hand, maybe a single pair or a busted draw. Betting 100 (the minimum raise) is too small and misses value. All-in is risky because it might only get called by a better hand (like a flush or full house). A raise of around 500-1000 seems reasonable, but I have to consider pot size and opponent's tendencies. Given the history, I've been aggressive, and they've called each time, so they might call a medium bet. I'll choose a raise of 800 to build the pot while not overcommitting.\n\nAnswer: 800"}
